@startuml BudgetDarpanMethodology
!include _theme.puml
title Budget Darpan — Development Methodology
caption Evidence-first agile delivery through complete vertical slices
left to right direction

rectangle "1. Discover" as Discover BLUESOFT {
  rectangle "Define civic problem" as D1
  rectangle "Study source portals" as D2
  rectangle "Identify trust risks" as D3
}

rectangle "2. Design" as Design TEAL {
  rectangle "Normalize relational model" as DS1
  rectangle "Define API and provenance" as DS2
  rectangle "Design bilingual UX" as DS3
}

rectangle "3. Build a Vertical Slice" as Build PURPLESOFT {
  rectangle "Working model" as B1
  rectangle "Working API" as B2
  rectangle "Working UI" as B3
  rectangle "Tests + demo integration" as B4
}

rectangle "4. Verify" as Verify #FFF1C5 {
  rectangle "Constraints and permissions" as V1
  rectangle "Citations and unknown states" as V2
  rectangle "Bilingual / accessibility checks" as V3
  rectangle "Regression and live smoke tests" as V4
}

rectangle "5. Review and Improve" as Improve #E8F4F1 {
  rectangle "Team review" as I1
  rectangle "Judge-critical feedback" as I2
  rectangle "Document limitations" as I3
  rectangle "Select next P0 slice" as I4
}

Discover --> Design
Design --> Build
Build --> Verify
Verify --> Improve
Improve -up-> Discover : next iteration

D1 --> D2
D2 --> D3
DS1 --> DS2
DS2 --> DS3
B1 --> B2
B2 --> B3
B3 --> B4
V1 --> V2
V2 --> V3
V3 --> V4
I1 --> I2
I2 --> I3
I3 --> I4

note bottom
  Priority order: data correctness → privacy/security → source traceability
  → demo-critical path → simplest professional implementation.
end note

legend bottom
  Each phase is complete only when model → API → UI → tests → demo work together.
  P0 stability comes before optional P1/P2 features.
endlegend
@enduml
